id: pm-rust-8qbo
title: "Resume native output-limit continuations after the last emitted row, matching pm-cli 2026.10.7"
description: "pm list --limit 50 --output-limit 30 returns 30 rows but next_cursor points after row 49 in the published CLI (2026.10.5 and 2026.10.6), so following it silently skips rows 30-49. pm-rust reproduces this byte-identically and pins it in tests/pagination_differential.rs bounded_receipts_match_bytes. When unbraind/pm-cli#1420 is fixed: bump COMPATIBLE_PM_VERSION, rebase the producer cursor to the last delivered row, and add a page-walk test asserting the union of delivered ids equals the full set."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: pagination,parity,upstream
created_at: "2026-10-06T18:04:22.824Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T22:08:20.241Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T18:39:14.821Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T18:39:14.821Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "Following next_cursor after an --output-limit trim delivers every row exactly once, in order, byte-identical to the fixed published CLI"
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T15:59:41.505Z",codex-sol,"Implement the published 2026.10.7 continuation contract, remove the producer-cursor defect pin, and add an exhaustive differential page walk with a native-only revert proof. Run the complete Linux release gate before review."
  "2026-10-07T16:04:51.452Z",codex-sol,"Published 2026.10.7 also fixes the shared combined-ceiling state: capture the uncapped snapshot and producer coordinates before amount trimming, then reuse them for budget rebasing and unchanged output-cursor replay. Differential assertions now require the correct snapshot and deleted-identity fallback. Preserve deliberate terminal caps; page walks exhaust them by lifting only the cap at the same incoming boundary."
  "2026-10-07T16:07:28.954Z",codex-sol,"Native-only revert proof: deleting only the amount-bound call to rebase_producer makes output_limit_producer_pages_are_complete_and_byte_identical fail with exit 101 against the unchanged lockfile-installed 2026.10.7 oracle. Restored the native fix. The fixed walk passed; it checks ordered full-list equality, unique IDs and decoded cursor boundaries under unbounded and nonbinding finite budgets."
  "2026-10-07T16:13:58.074Z",codex-sol,"The first complete release gate passed formatting, strict Clippy, rustdoc and all ordinary/instrumented tests, then correctly refused 99.84025559105432 percent branches and 99.97848537005164 percent regions. The sole gap was the amount-trim advertised-cursor branch in the library unit run. Added a direct positive test for an offset producer boundary, preserved snapshot fields, delivered counts and deliberate terminal caps under both nonbinding budget forms. Rerunning the unchanged 100 percent coverage gate."
  "2026-10-07T16:18:30.327Z",codex-sol,"Final Linux release gate passes via pm test --run --progress --match just release-check: cargo fmt, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, all-target/all-feature tests with required published parity, nightly llvm-cov, cargo audit and changelog verification. Coverage is 3069/3069 lines, 4648/4648 regions, 278/278 functions and 626/626 branches, all 100 percent. The 14 pagination tests include the complete cursor walk and updated combined-ceiling replay/deletion contracts. Native-only revert remains a proven exit-101 failure. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification and release the claim."
